と。","quotation":null,"display_id":10,"image_path":null,"legacy_ids":[],"provenance":{"note":"会話の順番交替を扱う原典。会話の連鎖全体の唯一の理論ではありません。","works":["A simplest systematics for the organization of turn-taking for conversation (1974). Language, 50(4), 696-735"],"period":"1974年（参照文献）","status":"書誌確認済み","sources":[{"url":"https://doi.org/10.2307/412243","title":"文献情報・原文（DOI）"}],"attribution":"Harvey Sacks / Emanuel A. Schegloff / Gail Jefferson（参照文献の著者）"},"updated_at":"2026-10-21T12:10:33.096605+00:00","updated_by":null,"access_tier":"complete","category_id":"practical-wisdom","canonical_id":"kb_464","display_order":10,"category_title":"実践知","knowledge_type":"method","subcategory_id":"practical-wisdom-c","taxonomy_order":10,"draft_relations":null,"draft_display_id":null,"related_theory_ids":[],"draft_technique_ids":[]},{"id":"kb_463","title":"タイミング効果","status":"published","aliases":[],"summary":"同じ言葉でも、伝える時機や会話の流れによって影響が変わること。","quotation":null,"display_id":11,"image_path":null,"legacy_ids":[],"provenance":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-21T12:10:33.096605+00:00","updated_by":null,"access_tier":"complete","category_id":"practical-wisdom","canonical_id":"kb_463","display_order":11,"category_title":"実践知","knowledge_type":"heuristic","subcategory_id":"practical-wisdom-c","taxonomy_order":11,"draft_relations":null,"draft_display_id":null,"related_theory_ids":[],"draft_technique_ids":[]},{"id":"kb_1045","title":"PREP法","status":"published","aliases":["PREP method"],"summary":"結論、理由、具体例、結論の順で、説明を組み立てる方法。\n「日程を変えたい。参加できない人が多いからだ。例えば今回は半数が欠席する。来週にずらしたい」のように組み立てる。","quotation":null,"display_id":12,"image_path":null,"legacy_ids":[],"provenance":{"note":"実務上の構成技法。由来や単一の発明者は断定しない。","works":["就職活動ハンドブック2025：相手に伝わる内容にしよう"],"status":"書誌確認済み","sources":[{"url":"https://www.aitech.ac.jp/assets/docs/career/for-students/center_for-students_handbook2025.pdf","title":"就職活動ハンドブック2025：相手に伝わる内容にしよう"}],"attribution":"愛知工業大学キャリアセンター（参照教材）"},"updated_at":"2026-10-21T12:10:33.096605+00:00","updated_by":null,"access_tier":"complete","category_id":"practical-wisdom","canonical_id":"kb_1045","display_order":12,"category_title":"実践知","knowledge_type":"method","subcategory_id":"practical-wisdom-c","taxonomy_order":12,"draft_relations":null,"draft_display_id":null,"related_theory_ids":["kb_394","kb_407","kb_1052"],"draft_technique_ids":[]},{"id":"kb_1046","title":"SBAR法","status":"published","aliases":["SBAR","situation-background-assessment-recommendation"],"summary":"状況、背景、自分の見立て、提案や依頼の順で、連絡する方法。\n急な欠員の連絡なら、今の状況、欠員の背景、業務への影響、応援の依頼の順に伝える。","quotation":null,"display_id":13,"image_path":null,"legacy_ids":[],"provenance":{"note":"医療発祥の連絡技法。一般業務の例は翻案。","works":["TeamSTEPPS: SBAR"],"status":"書誌確認済み","sources":[{"url":"https://www.ahrq.gov/teamstepps-program/curriculum/communication/tools/sbar.html","title":"TeamSTEPPS: SBAR"}],"attribution":"Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality"},"updated_at":"2026-10-21T12:10:33.096605+00:00","updated_by":null,"access_tier":"complete","category_id":"practical-wisdom","canonical_id":"kb_1046","display_order":13,"category_title":"実践知","knowledge_type":"method","subcategory_id":"practical-wisdom-c","taxonomy_order":13,"draft_relations":null,"draft_display_id":null,"related_theory_ids":["kb_435","kb_777","kb_1055","kb_1051"],"draft_technique_ids":[]},{"id":"kb_1047","title":"アイ・メッセージ","status":"published","aliases":["I-message","I-messages","私メッセージ"],"summary":"相手を決めつけず、自分の気持ちや受けた影響を主語にして伝える方法。\n「あなたは無責任だ」より、「連絡がないと、私は予定を組めず困る」のように伝える。","quotation":null,"display_id":14,"image_path":null,"legacy_ids":[],"provenance":{"note":"Gordonの方法を参照。相手の同意を得る保証や感情の押し付けの道具ではない。","works":["Origins of the Gordon Model"],"status":"書誌確認済み","sources":[{"url":"https://www.gordontraining.com/thomas-gordon/origins-of-the-gordon-model/","title":"Origins of the Gordon Model"}],"attribution":"Thomas Gordon / Gordon Training International"},"updated_at":"2026-10-21T12:10:33.096605+00:00","updated_by":null,"access_tier":"complete","category_id":"practical-wisdom","canonical_id":"kb_1047","display_order":14,"category_title":"実践知","knowledge_type":"method","subcategory_id":"practical-wisdom-c","taxonomy_order":14,"draft_relations":null,"draft_display_id":null,"related_theory_ids":["kb_404","kb_092","kb_052","kb_053","kb_008"],"draft_technique_ids":[]},{"id":"kb_1048","title":"SBIフィードバック","status":"published","aliases":["SBI feedback","situation-behavior-impact"],"summary":"状況、観察した行動、その影響の三つに絞って、評価や改善点を伝える方法。\n「昨日の会議で、話を最後まで聞いてくれたので、提案しやすかった」のように、行動と影響を結びつける。","quotation":null,"display_id":15,"image_path":null,"legacy_ids":[],"provenance":{"note":"開発元の定義を参照。効果の宣伝表現は採用しない。","works":["Situation–Behavior–Impact feedback（開発元の解説）"],"status":"書誌確認済み","sources":[{"url":"https://www.ccl.org/articles/leading-effectively-articles/closing-the-gap-between-intent-vs-impact-sbii/","title":"Situation–Behavior–Impact feedback（開発元の解説）"}],"attribution":"Center for Creative Leadership"},"updated_at":"2026-10-21T12:10:33.096605+00:00","updated_by":null,"access_tier":"complete","category_id":"practical-wisdom","canonical_id":"kb_1048","display_order":15,"category_title":"実践知","knowledge_type":"method","subcategory_id":"practical-wisdom-c","taxonomy_order":15,"draft_relations":null,"draft_display_id":null,"related_theory_ids":["kb_045","kb_424","kb_394"],"draft_technique_ids":[]},{"id":"kb_1049","title":"動機づけ面接","status":"published","aliases":["motivational interviewing"],"summary":"変化を押しつけず、本人の理由や価値観を引き出す対話の方法。","quotation":null,"display_id":16,"image_path":null,"legacy_ids":[],"provenance":{"note":"共同的な姿勢とプロセスを重視。医療・心理支援の代替として提示しない。","works":["Understanding Motivational Interviewing"],"status":"書誌確認済み","sources":[{"url":"https://motivationalinterviewing.org/understanding-motivational-interviewing","title":"Understanding Motivational Interviewing"}],"attribution":"William R. Miller / Stephen Rollnick；MINT"},"updated_at":"2026-10-21T12:10:33.096605+00:00","updated_by":null,"access_tier":"complete","category_id":"practical-wisdom","canonical_id":"kb_1049","dis